msgctxt "64"
msgid "So that's where that bastard ended up..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "76"
msgid ""
"Saw him around there on another shoot. And me, well, I never forget a "
"subject."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "112"
msgid "Outta my way!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "124"
msgid "(That's the kid who was looking for his dad. What's going on?)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "196"
msgid ""
"A journalist was just telling me about a photographer named Yanai. That you?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "208"
msgid ""
"Uh-huh. I'm a freelancer, but if I get any real moneymaker shots, I sell 'em"
" to the mags."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "220"
msgid ""
"And you're the Dragon of Dojima himself. I take it you sent the kid here?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "232"
msgid "I just saw him run out. What happened?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "244"
msgid "You remember this guy in the magazine photo? The one right behind you?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "280"
msgid ""
"He's Hirata, the president of Peace Finance. You got sent out to collect on "
"his debts fourteen years ago, in your early days."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "304"
msgid "A Hirata... from Peace Finance...? Oh yeah..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "388"
msgid ""
"I've been chasing scoops in Kamurocho a long time. But one story really "
"caught my eye... Yours. The Dragon of Dojima."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "400"
msgid ""
"You always had this strange intensity, even in the beginning. I could tell "
"you'd make it big someday."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "412"
msgid "Why's Hirata look so ragged now anyway? The guy looks like a vagrant."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "424"
msgid ""
"Well, you pushed him so hard to repay his debts, he lost face as a loan "
"shark. All his prospects in Kamurocho faded away."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "436"
msgid ""
"He lost everything, and ran off... leaving his family saddled with all the "
"debt he left behind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "448"
msgid "I see... So that guy was Hirata's son."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "460"
msgid "How do you know so much about Hirata, anyway?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "472"
msgid ""
"At the moment I took that photo... he was getting ready to stab you in the "
"back."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "484"
msgid "What!?"
msgstr "Cosa!?"

msgctxt "496"
msgid ""
"I suspected you'd been involved in the bombing, so I set myself up in "
"Kamurocho for a stakeout."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "508"
msgid ""
"Once he saw I had my camera trained on him, Hirata dropped the knife and ran"
" off."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "520"
msgid ""
"He had murder in his eyes that day... I could smell a story brewing, so I "
"went after him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "532"
msgid "And that's when he filled you in."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "544"
msgid ""
"Yep. It was too good a story to pass up. Journalist's gotta do what a "
"journalist's gotta do."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "556"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "568"
msgid "That kid planning on killing his old man?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "580"
msgid "What do you mean?"
msgstr "Cosa intendi?"

msgctxt "592"
msgid ""
"What, you didn't notice? He had a knife hidden in his breast pocket. And, "
"well..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "604"
msgid ""
"I know that look in his eyes. Same as his dad's, that day... He's out for "
"blood."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "616"
msgid "But why would he want to kill his dad?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "628"
msgid ""
"Hirata's debts tore his family apart. Sent his daughter out of college and "
"into sex work... and his wife died from the stress."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "640"
msgid ""
"Didn't do much to drive down the debt, though. The kid must have one hell of"
" a grudge... I doubt he's looking to talk it out."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "652"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "664"
msgid "Go. Stop him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "676"
msgid "What...?"
msgstr "Cosa...?"

msgctxt "688"
msgid ""
"You see a lot in my line of work. And I know Hirata's grudge against you "
"isn't rational."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "700"
msgid ""
"But those innocent folks wouldn't be wrapped up in all this if it wasn't for"
" you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "712"
msgid ""
"Seems fair to me. If you caused all this, the least you can do is help 'em."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "724"
msgid ""
"Besides... Nobody can just sit back and let a kid kill his dad. Not even "
"you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "736"
msgid "And you'll follow along, get your photos, and make a profit off it?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "748"
msgid ""
"Heh... Yeah, sounds about right. As long as someone's willing to buy the "
"story, I'll sell it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "760"
msgid "Where did Hirata's son go, anyway?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "772"
msgid ""
"West Park. You know, where all the homeless are. That's the old man's home "
"these days."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "784"
msgid "West Park, huh?"
msgstr ""

